<title>USA: American Travellers Corp Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>American Travellers Corp Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>BENSALEM, Pa. 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>For the three months ended September 30,</p>
<p>					 1996		1995  % Change</p>
<p> Revenues			     $108.3	    $68.3     59%</p>
<p> Net Income				9.2		5.7     61%</p>
<p> Primary EPS			     .54		.35     54%</p>
<p> Primary Shares			 17.0	     16.3	4%</p>
<p> Fully Diluted EPS_		    .43		.34     26%</p>
<p> Fully Diluted Shares		 23.9	     16.9     41%</p>
<p>For the nine months ended September 30,</p>
<p>					     1996	  1995  % Change</p>
<p> Revenues				   $317.8     $199.1     60%</p>
<p> Net Income				   26.0	 16.5     58%</p>
<p> Primary EPS				  1.55	 1.01     54%</p>
<p> Primary Shares			     16.8	 16.3	3%</p>
<p> Fully Diluted EPS			  1.24	 1.01     23%</p>
<p> Fully Diluted Shares		     23.8	 16.5     44%</p>
<p>NOTE: The company acquired the long term care insurance business from Transport Life Insurance Co and Continental Life Insurance Co, which was effective as of October 1, 1995. The acquisition added $22.3 million in premiums for the third quarter 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
